---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/NavBar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-11-15';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Americas Museums"
  description="How americasmuseums.com uses cookies, analytics, and third-party advertising; and how you can opt out of personalized ads."
>
  <NavBar slot="header" />

  <section class="bg-white border-b border-surface-line">
    <div class="max-w-content mx-auto px-5 py-10">
      <div class="text-2xs tracking-wider2 text-brand font-medium mb-2">LEGAL</div>
      <h1 class="display text-4xl text-ink mb-3 leading-tight">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-content mx-auto px-5 py-10 max-w-prose">
    <div class="prose-editorial">
      <h2>What this page covers</h2>
      <p>
        americasmuseums.com is an independent directory of American museums.
        We don't ask for accounts, don't collect personal information directly,
        and don't sell any data. This page explains the third-party services
        that run on the site and how you can opt out of personalized ads.
      </p>

      <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how visitors use the site
        (which pages are popular, how people get here, roughly where in the
        world traffic comes from). Google Analytics sets cookies and may
        collect your IP address, device type, and browsing behavior on this
        site. We configure Google Analytics with IP anonymization enabled.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can opt out of Google Analytics across all sites by installing
        the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google AdSense to display ads. <strong>Google, as a third-party
        vendor, uses cookies to serve ads on this site. Google's use of
        advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to our
        users based on their visit to this site and/or other sites on the
        Internet.</strong> Other third-party vendors or ad networks may also
        use cookies to serve ads on this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting Google's
        Ads Settings at
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">https://adssettings.google.com</a>.
        You can also opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for
        personalized advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some ticket links on museum pages are affiliate links — if you buy
        a ticket after clicking one, we may earn a small commission at no
        extra cost to you. Affiliate links are labeled near the button and
        use the <code>rel="sponsored nofollow"</code> attribute. These
        commissions help keep the site free.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies at a glance</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> <code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code> — measure site usage</li>
        <li><strong>Google AdSense:</strong> ad personalization and frequency capping cookies</li>
        <li><strong>Affiliate networks</strong> (GetYourGuide, Tiqets, etc.): may set cookies after you click a ticket link, to attribute a purchase back to this site</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The site is a general-audience travel directory. We don't knowingly
        collect personal information from children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent through the
        <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
